  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UN Coherence Effort 2011-2018 - UNDP Coherence Effort</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">UN Coherence Effort 2011-2018</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project &quot;Support to UN coherence efforts in Zimbabwe III&quot; has the overall objective of ensuring that the gains made by the UN in Zimbabwe during the implementation of phase I and II (2011-2018) are consolidated in a sustainable manner.
The project support the coherent implementation of the 2016-2020 ZUNDAF with a focus on Delivering as One, through increased joint programming efforts.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Sweden has supported the UNRCO since 2011. The original agreement for phase I was between 2011-2013. An addendum was made in February 2013 to support a phase II for another two years between April 2013 - April 2015. Two crucial posts have been recruited and fully funded during these years; a strategic planning specialist (also Head of UNRCO) and a communication specialist. Apart from these positions, the Swedish funding has also contributed to joint UN planning and implementation excercises during phase I and II. In the budget for phase II of the project, funds was secured for an in-depth project assessment, managed by UNRCO but carried out by an external consultant.

Given that the UN System in Zimbabwe is embarking on a new programme from 2016 to 2020, and in order for the UNCT to successfully fulfil its mandate, sustained coordination capacities in the UNRCO are essential. A three year strategy is therefore proposed, building on the Sweden supported project Support to UN coherence efforts in Zimbabwe phase I and II, whereby the human and technical resources of the UNRCO would be sustained and enhanced. With increased focus on joint programming, advocacy and communications, resources in this project will continue to significantly complement resources provided by other partners, UN Agencies in Zimbabwe and by UN Headquarters. In addition, this project will focus only on human resource capacity, with joint UN activities now funded only by UN HQ and the UN Country Team.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project&apos;s overall objective is to ensure that the necessary       capacities and resources are made available to the UN Resident        Coordinator and UN Country Team to better implement the Zimbabwe      United Nations Development Assistance Framework, by hiring a          Strategic Planning Advisor and a communication specialists.</narrative>
  </description>
